# A RELEASE, the minimal message of RFC 8415 section 18.2.7: the client identifier, the
# server identifier, elapsed time, and the IA_NA with the address being given back (the
# lifetimes are 0, the server ignores them). Documentation MAC 00:00:5e:00:53:02.
#
# msg-type RELEASE, transaction id 0x2a0003
08 2a 00 03
# option 1, client identifier, 10 octets: DUID-LL, hardware type 1, the MAC
00 01 00 0a
00 03 00 01 00 00 5e 00 53 02
# option 2, server identifier, 18 octets: DUID-UUID
00 02 00 12
00 04
00 11 22 33 44 55 46 77 88 99 aa bb cc dd ee ff
# option 8, elapsed time 0
00 08 00 02 00 00
# option 3, IA_NA, 40 octets: IAID 0x5e005302, T1 0, T2 0
00 03 00 28
5e 00 53 02
00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00
# option 5, IA Address, 24 octets: 2001:db8:1::100, lifetimes 0
00 05 00 18
20 01 0d b8 00 01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 01 00
00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00
